&= \frac{x^2 + y^2 + (y^2 - 1)^2 - x^2 - y^2}{2 \cdot \sqrt{x^2 + (y^2 - 1)^2} \cdot y} \\
&= \frac{y^2 - 1}{2y} \\
&= \boxed{\frac{y - \frac{1}{y}}{2}}.
\end{align*}. The answer is \frac{y-\frac1y}{2}

