The Shoelace Theorem states that if the vertices of a polygon are given in order, then the area of the polygon is equal to half the absolute value of the sum of the products of the coordinates of the vertices.
In this case, the vertices are given as $(4, -1)$, $(10, 3)$, and $(4, 5)$.
