$$\text{Area} = \frac{1}{2} |x_1y_2 + x_2y_3 + x_3y_1 - x_2y_1 - x_3y_2 - x_1y_3|$$
In this case, the vertices of the triangle are $(4, -1)$, $(10, 3)$, and $(4, 5)$. Plugging these values into the Shoelace Theorem, we get:
$$\text{Area} = \frac{1}{2} |4(3) + 10(5) + 4(-1) - 10(-1) - 4(3) - 4(5)|$$
$$\text{Area} = \frac{1}{2} |12 + 50 - 4 + 10 - 12 - 20|$$
$$\text{Area} = \frac{1}{2} |46|$$
$$\text{Area} = \boxed{23}$$
