Note that $f(2^{-x}) = f(2^x)$, since $f(2^x) + xf(2^{-x}) = 1$.  Thus, $f(2^{-x}) = f(2^x) = f(2^{|x|})$, and $f(2^x) = f(2^{|x|})$.  Since $f(2^x) + xf(2^{-x}) = 1$, $f(2^x) + xf(2^x) = 1$.  Let $y = 2^x$.  Then $f(y) + yf(\log_2 y) = 1$.  Let $g(x) = xf(\log_2 x)$.  Then $g(x) + g(-x) = 1$.  Let $h(x) = g(x) - g(-x)$.  Then $h(x) + h(-x) = 0$, so $h(x)$ is an even function.  Thus, $h(x) = h(-x)$.  Thus, $g(x) = g(-x)$.  Let $p = g(1)$.  Then $g(x) = p - xg(x)$, so $g(x) = \frac{p}{1 + x}$.  Then $f(2) = p - 2f(1)$, and $p = f(1) + f(2)$.  Thus, $f(2) = \boxed{\frac{1}{3}}$. The answer is \frac{1}{3}

