Let $p(x) = x^2 + ax + b.$  Then $|p(x)| \le 21$ for $-1 \le x \le 1$ if and only if $|x^2 + ax + b| \le 21$ for $-1 \le x \le 1.$  If $a^2 - 4b < 0,$ then $x^2 + ax + b$ is strictly increasing on $[-1,1].$  Therefore, $|x^2 + ax + b| \le |(-1)^2 + a(-1) + b| = |a + b - 1| = |a + b|.$  Thus, $|a + b| \le 21.$

If $a^2 - 4b \ge 0,$ then $x^2 + ax + b$ is strictly decreasing on $[-1,1].$  Therefore, $|x^2 + ax + b| \le |(-1)^2 + a(-1) + b| = |a + b - 1| = |a + b|.$  Thus, $|a + b| \le 21.$

Therefore, the smallest possible munificence of a monic quadratic polynomial is $\boxed{21}.$ The answer is 21

