p = \frac{10 \times 1}{\binom{40}{4}} = \frac{10}{\binom{40}{4}}
\]

### Step 2: Calculate \( q \)
The probability \( q \) is the probability that two of the slips bear a number \( a \) and the other two bear a number \( b \ne a \). There are 10 choices for the number \( a \) and 9 choices for the number \( b \)

