\[PA^2 + PB^2 + PC^2 - PH^2 = PA^2 + PB^2 + PC^2 - \frac{PA^2 + PB^2 + PC^2}{2} = \frac{1}{2} \left( (PA - PB)^2 + (PB - PC)^2 + (PC - PA)^2 \right) = \frac{1}{2} (2R^2 - 2R^2 \cos \angle BPC) = \frac{1}{2} (2R^2 - 2R^2 \cos \angle BAC).\]Then
\[PA^2 + PB^2 + PC^2 - PH^2 = R^2 \left( 1 - \frac{1}{2} \cos \angle BAC \right).\]Similarly, we can show that
\[PB^2 + PC^2 - PH^2 = R^2 \left( 1 - \frac{1}{2} \cos \angle BAC \right),\]and
\[PC^2 + PA^2 - PH^2 = R^2 \left( 1 - \frac{1}{2} \cos \angle BAC \right).\]Therefore, $PA^2 + PB^2 + PC^2 - PH^2$ is a constant equal to $R^2 \left( 1 - \frac{1}{2} \cos \angle BAC \right).$  From the Law of Cosines, we have
\begin{align*}
\cos \angle BAC &= \frac{b^2 + c^2 - a^2}{2bc} \\
