Let $p(x) = x^2 + ax + b.$  Then
\begin{align*}
|p(x)| &= |x^2 + ax + b| \\
&= |(x + \tfrac{a}{2})^2 + b - \tfrac{a^2}{4}| \\
&= |(x + \tfrac{a}{2})^2 + b - \tfrac{a^2}{4}| \\
&\le |(x + \tfrac{a}{2})^2| + |b - \tfrac{a^2}{4}| \\
&= (x + \tfrac{a}{2})^2 + |b - \tfrac{a^2}{4}|.
\end{align*}By AM-GM,
\[(x + \tfrac{a}{2})^2 + |b - \tfrac{a^2}{4}| \le \tfrac{1}{2}(|(x + \tfrac{a}{2})^2| + |b - \tfrac{a^2}{4}|). \quad \text{(1)}\]Also,
\begin{align*}
|x + \tfrac{a}{2}| &\le |x| + |\tfrac{a}{2}| \\
&\le 1 + |\tfrac{a}{2}| \\
&\le 1 + \tfrac{|a|}{2}.
\end{align*}Then
\begin{align*}
|x + \tfrac{a}{2}|^2 &\le (1 + \tfrac{|a|}{2})^2 \\
&= 1 + 2\tfrac{|a|}{2} + \tfrac{|a|^2}{4} \\
&= 1 + |a| + \tfrac{|a|^2}{4}.
\end{align*}Therefore,
\begin{align*}
|x + \tfrac{a}{2}|^2 + |b - \tfrac{a^2}{4}| &\le 1 + |a| + \tfrac{|a|^2}{4} + |b - \tfrac{a^2}{4}| \\
&= 1 + |a| + \tfrac{|a|^2}{4} + |b| - \tfrac{a^2}{4} \\
&= 1 + |a| + |b| - \tfrac{3}{4}|a|^2.
\end{align*}Thus, the munificence of $p(x)$ is at most
\[1 + |a| + |b| - \tfrac{3}{4}|a|^2.\]We want to minimize this munificence.  If $|a| \ge 2,$ then
\[1 + |a| + |b| - \tfrac{3}{4}|a|^2 \ge 1 + 2 + |b| - \tfrac{3}{4}(4) = 5 + |b| - 3 = 2 + |b|.\]If $|a| < 2,$ then
\[1 + |a| + |b| - \tfrac{3}{4}|a|^2 = 1 + |a| + |b| - \tfrac{3}{4}|a|^2\]is minimized when $|b|$ is minimized, and this minimum value is 0.  Therefore, the smallest possible munificence of a monic quadratic polynomial is $2.$

