By the Pythagorean Theorem, $BC = \sqrt{61-25} = \sqrt{36} = 6$. Let $O$ be the center of the circle. By the Pythagorean Theorem, $OB^2 + OC^2 = 61$. Since $OB = OP = r$, we have $OC^2 = 61 - 2r^2$.

