By the Law of Cosines on triangle $ACD,$
\[AC^2 = x^2 + (x \sqrt{3})^2 - 2x^2 \cos \angle CAD = x^2 + 3x^2 - 2x^2 \cdot 2x \cos 30^\circ = 2x^2 - 3x^2 \sqrt{3} = x^2(2 - 3\sqrt{3}).\]By the Law of Cosines on triangle $BCD,$
\[BD^2 = x^2 + (x \sqrt{3})^2 - 2x^2 \cos \angle CBD = x^2 + 3x^2 - 2x^2 \cdot 2y \cos 30^\circ = x^2 + 3x^2 - 2x^2 \cdot 2y \sqrt{3} = x^2(4 - 6y \sqrt{3}).\]Therefore,
\begin{align*}
AB^2 &= BD^2 + AC^2 \\
&= x^2(4 - 6y \sqrt{3}) + x^2(2 - 3\sqrt{3}) \\
&= x^2(4 - 6y \sqrt{3} + 2 - 3\sqrt{3}) \\
&= x^2(6 - 9 \sqrt{3}y).
\end{align*}Thus, $AB = x \sqrt{6 - 9 \sqrt{3}y}.$

By the Law of Cosines on triangle $ABC,$
\[AC^2 = AB^2 + BC^2 - 2AB \cdot BC \cos \angle ACB = x^2(6 - 9 \sqrt{3}y) + x^2(6 - 9 \sqrt{3}y) - 2x \cdot x \sqrt{6 - 9 \sqrt{3}y} \cdot x \sqrt{6 - 9 \sqrt{3}y} \cos \angle ACB.\]Therefore,
\[\cos \angle ACB = \frac{x^2(6 - 9 \sqrt{3}y) + x^2(6 - 9 \sqrt{3}y) - 2x^2(6 - 9 \sqrt{3}y)}{2x^2(6 - 9 \sqrt{3}y)} = \frac{6 - 9 \sqrt{3}y}{2(6 - 9 \sqrt{3}y)} = \boxed{\frac{3}{2(3 - \sqrt{3})}}.\]. The answer is \frac{3}{2(3-\sqrt{3})}

