\begin{array}{cl}
k + 3 & \text{if $k$ is odd}, \\
\frac{k}{2} & \text{if $k$ is even}.
\end{array}
\right.\]Since $k$ is odd, $f(k) = k + 3.$  Then \[f(f(k)) = f(k + 3) = \frac{k + 3}{2}.\]Since $k$ is odd, $f(f(k)) = \frac{k + 3}{2}$ is even.  Therefore, \[f(f(f(k))) = f\left(\frac{k + 3}{2}\right) = \frac{k + 3}{2} + 3 = \frac{k + 13}{2}.\]Since $f(f(f(k))) = 27,$ we have \[\frac{k + 13}{2} = 27.\]Then $k + 13 = 54,$ so $k = \boxed{41}.$. The answer is 41

